WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:03.968
-Stephanie, welcome.
It is so great to meet you.

00:00:03.968 --> 00:00:05.367
-It's so nice to meet you too.

00:00:05.367 --> 00:00:07.501
-Really, and what a knockout
performance in this movie.

00:00:07.501 --> 00:00:09.901
Congratulations on that.
-Thank you.

00:00:09.901 --> 00:00:12.100
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thank you so much.

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:14.200
-First, congratulations,
the cast of

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:16.434
"Everything Everywhere All at
Once" had a big night

00:00:16.434 --> 00:00:17.801
at the SAG Awards.
-Yes.

00:00:17.801 --> 00:00:19.501
-I mean, really.
That was fantastic.

00:00:19.501 --> 00:00:23.968
But I liked this. The camera
came over to you and you were

00:00:23.968 --> 00:00:25.868
holding -- you looked at the
camera and you were holding,

00:00:25.868 --> 00:00:28.701
like, what is this?
A silver -- What is it? A ball?

00:00:28.701 --> 00:00:31.167
-Who is that intense person?
-Look at how fun.

00:00:31.167 --> 00:00:32.801
-It's me!
-You gotta have fun.

00:00:32.801 --> 00:00:34.167
Come on, yeah. How fun.

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:35.634
But what does that mean?
What is this?

00:00:35.634 --> 00:00:38.467
-Yeah, so, Jamie Lee Curtis is
like our biggest cheerleader,

00:00:38.467 --> 00:00:41.567
and her biggest love language is
gift giving.

00:00:41.567 --> 00:00:45.734
And so right before the category
came out, she ran around

00:00:45.734 --> 00:00:48.567
to the whole cast, and she gave
this little ball to us,

00:00:48.567 --> 00:00:49.868
that's like a little rock,

00:00:49.868 --> 00:00:51.934
so that no one would leave
empty-handed.

00:00:51.934 --> 00:00:53.834
-Come on!
-I know. We love it.

00:00:53.834 --> 00:00:55.934
-Come on.
That's the awesome Jamie Lee.

00:00:55.934 --> 00:00:57.334
But you did -- No one left
empty-handed.

00:00:57.334 --> 00:00:59.834
-No, no. In fact, a SAG Award is
very heavy.

00:00:59.834 --> 00:01:02.601
-Yeah. You guys crushed it.
That was great.

00:01:02.601 --> 00:01:05.968
How does it feel? How does all
these accolades feel?

00:01:05.968 --> 00:01:09.234
-You know, this movie
is so special to me.

00:01:09.234 --> 00:01:10.567
We filmed in 2020.

00:01:10.567 --> 00:01:14.234
I knew then that it was the most
special experience

00:01:14.234 --> 00:01:16.334
I've ever had creatively
in my life.

00:01:16.334 --> 00:01:20.300
I knew then that it was amazing,
and then, you know, we put it

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:23.701
on hold for two years and then
premiered at South by Southwest.

00:01:23.701 --> 00:01:26.100
And then that was amazing to
finally get to share it.

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:27.767
The reception was amazing.

00:01:27.767 --> 00:01:30.868
So, it's just been, like, stacks
on stacks on stacks

00:01:30.868 --> 00:01:34.701
of just incredible,
incredible journey.

00:01:34.701 --> 00:01:37.000
-And now you're nominated for
an Academy Award.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:38.133
-"Ohscar."
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:38.133 --> 00:01:39.367
-An Ohscar.
-Ohscar.

00:01:39.367 --> 00:01:40.667
-Ohscar.
-Ohscar. Yeah.

00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:43.367
-You're nominated for an Oscar.
-Yes.

00:01:43.367 --> 00:01:45.434
-Where did you find out that you
got nominated?

00:01:45.434 --> 00:01:47.033
Where were you?
-I was on an airplane.

00:01:47.033 --> 00:01:49.834
I've been shooting this movie
called "The Fall Guy,"

00:01:49.834 --> 00:01:53.367
David Leitch's next film, with
Ryan Gosling and Emily Blunt.

00:01:53.367 --> 00:01:54.400
And so I've been --
[ Applause ]

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:56.033
Yeah.
It's gonna be very special.

00:01:56.033 --> 00:01:58.968
-Wow! Yeah, no big deal.
Yeah, come back for that.

00:01:58.968 --> 00:02:02.367
-Yeah. And I've been commuting
to Sydney, which has been --

00:02:02.367 --> 00:02:03.901
-What?
-Sydney is far, it turns out.

00:02:03.901 --> 00:02:06.400
-Yeah, you don't commute to
Australia.

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:07.434
-But I have been.

00:02:07.434 --> 00:02:09.033
-Wow, thank you for being here
tonight.

00:02:09.033 --> 00:02:12.067
-Yeah. And I found out
on the plane.

00:02:12.067 --> 00:02:15.501
And I knew I was gonna be flying
back from Sydney to L.A.

00:02:15.501 --> 00:02:17.734
the day of the announcements.

00:02:17.734 --> 00:02:21.167
And I wanted to do a ritual for
myself to --

00:02:21.167 --> 00:02:23.267
You know, things have gotten
shinier and shinier.

00:02:23.267 --> 00:02:25.767
And I wanted to have a moment
where I got to watch the movie

00:02:25.767 --> 00:02:28.868
one more time to look back on
that moment of

00:02:28.868 --> 00:02:30.901
that seed of making,
the heartbeat,

00:02:30.901 --> 00:02:32.734
this very special thing
we made together.

00:02:32.734 --> 00:02:34.901
And I hadn't watched it
on a plane.

00:02:34.901 --> 00:02:37.234
So, before the announcements
came out,

00:02:37.234 --> 00:02:38.801
I watched it on the plane.

00:02:38.801 --> 00:02:41.968
And I felt like one of those
superfans of our own movie

00:02:41.968 --> 00:02:43.934
where they always say,
"You know, the movie starts

00:02:43.934 --> 00:02:45.133
and I just start weeping."

00:02:45.133 --> 00:02:47.033
And that was me.
And I was so embarrassed.

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:49.601
I was like, "I hope no one's
seeing me cry at our own movie."

00:02:49.601 --> 00:02:50.934
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.934 --> 00:02:53.400
-You're watching your own movie,
crying.

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:54.734
"What a performance!"

00:02:54.734 --> 00:02:56.300
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:57.968
"Isn't she fantastic?"

00:02:57.968 --> 00:03:00.100
-It was before I even came on.

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:03.200
There's this opening montage
where we're in a mirror

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:05.901
and you see the family --
the mother, the daughter,

00:03:05.901 --> 00:03:09.167
and the husband --
just singing karaoke together.

00:03:09.167 --> 00:03:11.434
And I literally started weeping,
and I was like,

00:03:11.434 --> 00:03:13.901
"They have no idea what's about
to happen to them."

00:03:13.901 --> 00:03:15.467
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.467 --> 00:03:17.734
"They don't even know!"
You know?

00:03:17.734 --> 00:03:19.400
-And then you get nominated.
-Yes.

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:21.234
Like, right as
we're about to land,

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:23.033
my phone started to go off.
-Yep.

00:03:23.033 --> 00:03:25.534
-And I was like, "Oh, my God,
what's happening?"

00:03:25.534 --> 00:03:28.734
And I just kind of like sat in
the little hovel

00:03:28.734 --> 00:03:31.834
by myself being like,
"What's going on?"

00:03:31.834 --> 00:03:35.267
And the flight attendant came up
to me, and she was like,

00:03:35.267 --> 00:03:37.334
"You've been so quiet
this whole trip.

00:03:37.334 --> 00:03:39.167
You're such an incredible
passenger."

00:03:39.167 --> 00:03:42.334
I was like, "Yeah, thanks,
I commute to Sydney."

00:03:42.334 --> 00:03:46.734
And she was like, "And you're so
smart to bring 'everything.'"

00:03:46.734 --> 00:03:48.968
And I was like, "Oh, my God.
Does she know?"

00:03:48.968 --> 00:03:51.467
But I think she was referring
to the fact

00:03:51.467 --> 00:03:53.033
that I always pack my own lunch.

00:03:53.033 --> 00:03:54.567
[ Laughter ]

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:56.000
-So she had no idea?
-She had no idea who I was.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:57.734
-You were like, "Did you catch
me watching my own --"

00:03:57.734 --> 00:03:59.968
She's like, "You brought
'everything.'

00:03:59.968 --> 00:04:02.434
Everywhere. All at once."

00:04:02.434 --> 00:04:03.567
Then you go --
-Salad.

00:04:03.567 --> 00:04:05.767
-Salad. Yeah, exactly.
-Exactly.

00:04:05.767 --> 00:04:07.801
-Congrats again. That is so rad.

00:04:07.801 --> 00:04:14.100
You are kind of -- It's an
unbelievable character role

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:16.767
for someone to play, but here
you are as Joy.

00:04:16.767 --> 00:04:17.968
-Yes.
-Okay?

00:04:17.968 --> 00:04:21.067
And then here you are as Jobu.

00:04:21.067 --> 00:04:22.434
-Yes.

00:04:22.434 --> 00:04:23.801
[ Audience oohs ]
-Yeah, ooh, exactly.

00:04:23.801 --> 00:04:25.934
-Oh. [ Laughs ]

00:04:25.934 --> 00:04:27.734
-I mean, you crush
when you're Jobu.

00:04:27.734 --> 00:04:29.968
I mean, you just like do
everything.

00:04:29.968 --> 00:04:32.601
What was the direction like
when you're on set?

00:04:32.601 --> 00:04:34.634
-Yeah, the Daniels and I,
we had worked together

00:04:34.634 --> 00:04:37.667
right before this movie,
and we're all very weird.

00:04:37.667 --> 00:04:40.634
And I have no fear of being
weird with them.

00:04:40.634 --> 00:04:43.667
And in fact, they kind of bring
out more weird in me.

00:04:43.667 --> 00:04:46.868
So, when we were kind of working
on the role, we would really

00:04:46.868 --> 00:04:49.100
start to, like, you know, get
into it.

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:51.501
And they would give me
the direction a lot like,

00:04:51.501 --> 00:04:53.868
"Okay, now, break the movie.
Destroy the movie."

00:04:53.868 --> 00:04:55.934
And so I would do a scene --
-Break the movie?

00:04:55.934 --> 00:04:58.634
-I would do a scene as Jobu, as
written, and sometimes I would

00:04:58.634 --> 00:05:02.467
just stop or sometimes I would
just, like, leave frame.

00:05:02.467 --> 00:05:05.033
But this is when we were working
just the three of us.

00:05:05.033 --> 00:05:07.200
And then the first day I got
into set, it was

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:09.701
the hallway scene where --
the introduction of Jobu.

00:05:09.701 --> 00:05:11.734
-You're wearing the Elvis suit.
-The Elvis suit.

00:05:11.734 --> 00:05:13.901
The schling schlings and the --
You know, if you've seen

00:05:13.901 --> 00:05:15.601
the movie, you know what
schling schlings are.

00:05:15.601 --> 00:05:18.300
-Yeah, thank you, I appreciate
you editing for us.

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:19.834
-Yeah. You're welcome.
-The schling schlings.

00:05:19.834 --> 00:05:23.334
-The schling schlings.
-Sure, yeah, I understand.

00:05:23.334 --> 00:05:27.601
-And all of a sudden, I got so
nervous because it was

00:05:27.601 --> 00:05:30.534
my first scene with Michelle
Yeoh and I had never worked with

00:05:30.534 --> 00:05:32.634
any of the crew,
and so I was like,

00:05:32.634 --> 00:05:35.934
"They're going to think I'm
the worst actor on Earth.

00:05:35.934 --> 00:05:38.067
They're going to think
that I'm being weird

00:05:38.067 --> 00:05:40.267
and completely unhinged
for no reason."

00:05:40.267 --> 00:05:42.100
So I made them make
an announcement.

00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:44.334
I made them make an announcement
to the whole crew,

00:05:44.334 --> 00:05:46.767
and just be like, "Hey,
everybody, this is Stephanie.

00:05:46.767 --> 00:05:48.501
She's going to be kind of weird.

00:05:48.501 --> 00:05:49.667
[ Laughter ]

00:05:49.667 --> 00:05:50.567
-She's "acting." She's acting.

00:05:50.567 --> 00:05:52.334
-"But we told her to do that."

00:05:52.334 --> 00:05:55.734
-Okay, yeah. And then
this person walks out.

00:05:55.734 --> 00:05:57.400
And you crushed it.
-Thank you.

00:05:57.400 --> 00:06:01.267
-I gotta say, right -- almost
exactly when it came out,

00:06:01.267 --> 00:06:04.200
it barely was out,
Questlove was like,

00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:06.400
"Dude, this is the --
this is the movie."

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:11.634
-Well, Questlove was my most
special and kind of first big,

00:06:11.634 --> 00:06:15.701
like, celebrity introduction,
where he came to

00:06:15.701 --> 00:06:16.934
a screening we were doing.

00:06:16.934 --> 00:06:18.767
And I had heard --
like, word on the block was

00:06:18.767 --> 00:06:20.534
that Questlove really loved
the movie.

00:06:20.534 --> 00:06:23.534
And so, I saw him come into
the screening, and I was like,

00:06:23.534 --> 00:06:25.234
"If there was ever a chance

00:06:25.234 --> 00:06:28.033
that I could say hi to
Questlove, it's now."

00:06:28.033 --> 00:06:30.033
So I, like, walked right up to
him, and I was like,

00:06:30.033 --> 00:06:33.133
"Hi. I'm Stephanie.
Thank you for being here."

00:06:33.133 --> 00:06:34.734
-Yeah.
-And he was amazing.

00:06:34.734 --> 00:06:36.501
And it was -- But I --
And then I walked away --

00:06:36.501 --> 00:06:37.968
I didn't tell you this part.
But I walked away

00:06:37.968 --> 00:06:39.801
and I was like,
"What did I just do?"

00:06:39.801 --> 00:06:41.200
[ Laughter ]

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:43.934
"Wow, I'm so strong."
-Yeah, you really are.

00:06:43.934 --> 00:06:46.734
I want to show a clip.
Here's Stephanie Hsu in

00:06:46.734 --> 00:06:48.367
"Everything Everywhere
All at Once."

00:06:48.367 --> 00:06:50.000
Take a look at this.

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:53.434
-Is it that I "can't" be here?

00:06:56.434 --> 00:06:58.901
Or that I'm not "allowed"
to be here?

00:06:58.901 --> 00:07:00.100
-Hey!

00:07:01.133 --> 00:07:03.234
-Okay.

00:07:03.234 --> 00:07:06.968
Hands where I can see them.
-See, I can physically be here.

00:07:08.834 --> 00:07:10.267
But what you meant to say

00:07:10.267 --> 00:07:13.200
is you're not allowing me
to be here.

00:07:13.934 --> 00:07:15.667
[ Laughter ]

00:07:15.667 --> 00:07:17.434
-Hands behind your back.
Come on.

00:07:19.934 --> 00:07:22.400
-You're gonna make me walk
through you?

00:07:22.400 --> 00:07:25.601
-[ Snickers ] Yeah, cute.
Can't let you do that either.

00:07:25.601 --> 00:07:27.934
-Again with the "can't"!

00:07:29.734 --> 00:07:31.434
See, I don't think you
understand

00:07:31.434 --> 00:07:33.267
the meaning of that word.

00:07:41.534 --> 00:07:43.200
-Oh, my gosh. Come on.

00:07:43.200 --> 00:07:44.667
Stephanie Hsu.

00:07:44.667 --> 00:07:47.801
"Everything Everywhere All at
Once" is out now.

